</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kollmann</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Rafolt</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Nowotny</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ewers</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Bergmann</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Systematic distortions in magnetic position digitizers</article-title><source>Med Phys</source><year>1998</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>2242</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9829253</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1118/1.598425</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Intra-operative position sensing and tracking devices</article-title><source>Proceedings of the First Joint CVRMed/MRCAS Conference</source><year>1997</year><fpage>62</fpage><lpage>64</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Stokes</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Three-dimensional terminology of spinal deformity. A report presented to the Scoliosis Research Society by the Scoliosis Research Society Working Group on 3-D terminology of spinal deformity</article-title><source>Spine</source><year>1994</year><volume>19</volume><fpage>236</fpage><lpage>48</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8153835</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cheriet</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Delorme</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Dansereau</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Aubin</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></name><name><surname>de Guise</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Labelle</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>[Perioperative radiographic reconstruction of the scoliotic vertebral column]</article-title><source>Ann Chir</source><year>1999</year><volume>53</volume><fpage>808</fpage><lpage>15</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10584393</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Delorme</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Labelle</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Poitras</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Rivard</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Coillard</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Dansereau</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pre-, intra-, and postoperative three-dimensional evaluation of adolescent idiopathic scoliosis</article-title><source>J Spinal Disord</source><year>2000</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>93</fpage><lpage>101</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10780682</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1097/00002517-200004000-00001</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Callahan</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Brown</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Positioning techniques in spinal surgery</article-title><source>Clin Orthop</source><year>1981</year><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7471559</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kramers-de Quervain</surname><given-names>IA</given-names></name><name><surname>M&#x000fc;ller</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Stacoff</surname><given-names>A<